AB  - Reading the memoir Poor reinforced the vastness and complexity of poverty – an issue that still blights the lives of countless young people today, says Sarah Schofield Adrian Chiles's emotional response to Poor by Katriona O'Sullivan really resonated with me ( I'd never cried during a live broadcast – then three poignant words had me sobbing, 30 July ). I read it and my heart both sobbed and cheered for Katriona's younger self and the woman she has become. With its linear narrative, rich cultural references and "rags-to-riches" form, it might be taken for a tale of "that was then but this is…
